[00:42.11] It started with a dedication
[00:44.58] 'Lost in admiration - happy birthday -
[00:47.95] I'm forever yours - blossom
[00:50.91] Fared red inside a tiny book of butterflies
[00:54.73] I smiled surprised at how when flickered through
[00:58.51] The wings flew by spelled out my name
[01:02.97] Six months went by the summer lost
[01:05.89] Obsessively the letters dropped into my life
[01:09.60] The same soft blood smooth flowing hand
[01:13.19] Please try to understand - I have to see you - have to feel you -
[01:17.03] Tell you all the ways I need you - yours forever in love
[01:24.73] Strange attraction spreads it's wings
[01:27.28] It varies but the smallest things
[01:29.65] You never know how anything will change
[01:35.24] Strange attraction spreads it's wings
[01:38.00] And alters but the smallest things
[01:40.49] You never know how anything will fade
[01:44.95] 
[01:56.22] The year grew old incessantly she wrote to me
[02:00.58] She'd started smoking poetry!
[02:03.05] I laughed in recognition of a favorite phrase
[02:07.12] She'd pulled me in...
[02:08.31] I answered her
[02:09.72] A christmas card in sepia
[02:12.09] Arranging when and where
[02:14.47] And how the two of us should meet...
[02:18.35] Her opening so well prepared
[02:20.44] A nervous smile
[02:21.81] I couldn't take my eyes from her
[02:24.35] She whisperes
[02:25.90] Can I use some of your lipstick?
[02:28.49] It was perfect so believable
[02:31.06] I couldn't help but feel that it was real
[02:34.79] And kissing crimson fell into her waiting arms
[02:39.04] Strange attraction spreads it's wings
[02:41.68] It varies but the smallest things
[02:44.22] You never know how anything will change
[02:49.55] Strange attraction spreads it's wings
[02:52.36] And alters but the smallest things
[02:54.81] You never know how anything will fade
[03:01.69] 
[03:11.25] So alone into the cold new year without another word from her
[03:16.15] I wrote to ask if we could maybe meet again before the spring
[03:21.83] But weeks went by with no reply untill once more my birthday came
[03:26.98] And with it my surprise but this time nothing was the same...
[03:32.64] I'm sorry - blame infatuation - blame imagination
[03:37.79] I was sure you'd be the one but I was wrong -
[03:41.72] It seems reality destroys our dreams - I won't forget you blossom
[03:46.34] Fared red inside a tiny book of old goodbyes...
